§ `Sch 1 cll 38C, 38D -- rent assistance`

-- Single, $15,000 rent: (15,000 - 5,000.50) / 4 x 3 = $7,499.63, above Rate B for 1 or 2 children: $6,343.70.
#ASSERT `How much rent assistance do I get a year` `printed figures` `a single parent with two children under 13, income 30000` `rent of 15000` EQUALS `an amount` 6343.70
-- $10,000 rent: (10,000 - 5,000.50) / 4 x 3 = $3,749.625.
#ASSERT `How much rent assistance do I get a year` `printed figures` `a single parent with two children under 13, income 30000` `rent of 10000` EQUALS `an amount` 3749.625
-- $4,000 rent is not "more than" $5,000.50 a year: none.
#ASSERT `How much rent assistance do I get a year` `printed figures` `a single parent with two children under 13, income 30000` `rent of 4000` EQUALS `an amount` 0
-- A member of a couple, $12,000 rent: (12,000 - 7,391.25) / 4 x 3 = $3,456.5625.
#ASSERT `How much rent assistance do I get a year` `printed figures` `a couple with three children, family income 50000` `rent of 12000, couple` EQUALS `an amount` 3456.5625
-- The same couple separated by illness takes the single threshold: (12,000 - 5,000.50) / 4 x 3 = $5,249.625.
#ASSERT `How much rent assistance do I get a year` `printed figures` `a couple with three children, family income 50000` `rent of 12000, couple separated by illness` EQUALS `an amount` 5249.625
-- Three rent assistance children, $20,000 rent: $9,456.56 by the formula, above Rate B for 3 or more children: $7,168.60.
#ASSERT `How much rent assistance do I get a year` `printed figures` `a couple with three children, family income 50000` `rent of 20000, both partners receive maintenance` EQUALS `an amount` 7168.60
-- A relevant shared carer is under cl 38E, which is not encoded.
#ASSERT `How much rent assistance do I get a year` `printed figures` `a single parent with two children under 13, income 30000` `a relevant shared carer paying rent` EQUALS `not covered`

§ `Sch 1 cll 19B-22 -- the maintenance income test`

-- $2,000 received over 73 days, annualised: 2,000 x 365 / 73 = $10,000.
#ASSERT `What is my annualised maintenance income` `rent of 10000 and 2000 maintenance over 73 days` EQUALS 10000
-- Free area, single with two FTB children: $952.65 + $317.55 = $1,270.20.
#ASSERT `What is my maintenance income free area` `printed figures` `a single parent with two children under 13, income 30000` `rent of 10000 and 2000 maintenance over 73 days` EQUALS 1270.20
-- Both partners receive maintenance, three children: $1,905.30 + 2 x $317.55 = $2,540.40.
#ASSERT `What is my maintenance income free area` `printed figures` `a couple with three children, family income 50000` `rent of 20000, both partners receive maintenance` EQUALS 2540.40
-- Reduction: half of ($10,000 - $1,270.20) = $4,364.90.
#ASSERT `What is my reduction for maintenance income` `printed figures` `a single parent with two children under 13, income 30000` `rent of 10000 and 2000 maintenance over 73 days` EQUALS `an amount` 4364.90
-- A blind age or disability support pensioner: nil (cl 19B).
#ASSERT `What is my reduction for maintenance income` `printed figures` `a single parent with two children under 13, income 30000` `40000 maintenance for the year, blind pensioner` EQUALS `an amount` 0
-- Two maintenance payers bring in the ceilings of Subdivisions C and D: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is my reduction for maintenance income` `printed figures` `a single parent with two children under 13, income 30000` `maintenance from two payers` EQUALS `not covered`

§ `Sch 1 cll 3, 25 -- FTB Part A with rent assistance and maintenance`

-- With no rent and no maintenance the answer is the one fa-families.l4 gives: $2,016.20 for Chloe and Liam (c064).
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part A do I get a year with rent and maintenance` `printed` `printed figures` `Chloe and Liam with Oliver, family income 70000` `no rent and no maintenance` EQUALS `an amount` 2016.20
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part A do I get a year` `printed` `Chloe and Liam with Oliver, family income 70000` EQUALS 2016.20
-- Single, two children under 13, $30,000 (no income excess): maximum rate 2 x $4,292.40 + 2 x $600 = $9,784.80, plus $6,343.70
-- rent assistance: $16,128.50.
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part A do I get a year with rent and maintenance` `printed` `printed figures` `a single parent with two children under 13, income 30000` `rent of 15000` EQUALS `an amount` 16128.50
-- $9,784.80 + $3,749.625 - $4,364.90 = $9,169.525.
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part A do I get a year with rent and maintenance` `printed` `printed figures` `a single parent with two children under 13, income 30000` `rent of 10000 and 2000 maintenance over 73 days` EQUALS `an amount` 9169.525
-- $40,000 maintenance: the reduction of $19,364.90 takes the rate below the base rate, 2 x $1,416.20 + 2 x $600 = $4,032.40.
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part A do I get a year with rent and maintenance` `printed` `printed figures` `a single parent with two children under 13, income 30000` `40000 maintenance for the year` EQUALS `an amount` 4032.40
-- The blind pensioner keeps the full $9,784.80.
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part A do I get a year with rent and maintenance` `printed` `printed figures` `a single parent with two children under 13, income 30000` `40000 maintenance for the year, blind pensioner` EQUALS `an amount` 9784.80
-- Couple, three children, $50,000: $14,677.20 maximum less 20% of $10,000 = $12,677.20, plus $3,456.5625 rent assistance:
-- $16,133.7625.
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part A do I get a year with rent and maintenance` `printed` `printed figures` `a couple with three children, family income 50000` `rent of 12000, couple` EQUALS `an amount` 16133.7625
-- The same with $20,000 rent and $3,000 maintenance to both: $12,677.20 + $7,168.60 - half of ($3,000 - $2,540.40) = $19,616.
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part A do I get a year with rent and maintenance` `printed` `printed figures` `a couple with three children, family income 50000` `rent of 20000, both partners receive maintenance` EQUALS `an amount` 19616
-- Method 2 (couple, $100,000): the Method 2 comparison rate with rent assistance is 4,292.40 + 3,456.5625 - 11,797.60 - 303.60,
-- below nil, so the provisional rate of $1,112.60 stands, as in fa-families.l4.
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part A do I get a year with rent and maintenance` `printed` `printed figures` `a couple with one child, family income 100000` `rent of 12000, couple` EQUALS `an amount` 1112.60
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part A do I get a year with rent and maintenance` `printed` `printed figures` `a single parent with two children under 13, income 30000` `maintenance from two payers` EQUALS `not covered`

§ `Sch 4 cll 4-6 -- indexation`

-- 140 / 136 = 1.02941: 1.029. 137.5 / 130 = 1.05769: raised to 1.058. 130 / 135: 1.
#ASSERT `What is the FTB indexation factor` 140 136 EQUALS 1.029
#ASSERT `What is the FTB indexation factor` 137.5 130 EQUALS 1.058
#ASSERT `What is the FTB indexation factor` 130 135 EQUALS 1
-- The FTB child rate under 13, $4,292.40 x 1.029 = $4,416.88, to the nearest $3.65: $4,416.50 (1,210 x $3.65).
#ASSERT `What is the FTB indexed amount` 4292.40 140 136 3.65 EQUALS 4416.50
